  publisher = "7 Experiences Society",
  abstract  = "This study investigates cruise experience preferences through a
               hierarchical cluster analysis of budget-constrained choices. The
               research identifies three distinct passenger segments by
               surveying potential cruise passengers: Experience-Focused Luxury
               Cruisers, Entertainment and Relaxation Seekers, and Active
               Explorer Cruisers. Each segment demonstrates unique spending
               patterns and prioritization of cruise experience dimensions, such
               as cabin preferences, service expectations, food and beverage
               options, relaxation activities, and entertainment. The findings
               reveal that Experience-Focused Luxury Cruisers prioritize premium
               drinks and luxury experiences; Entertainment and relaxation
               Seekers focus on onboard entertainment and relaxation, while
